New adventuring skill: mine.

1) Mine cuts ore out of a rock face.
   - You need a pick in hand and hills, mountains or a cave around you.
   - Sewers hold nothing worth having, whatever their depth.

2) What the rock holds depends on where you are and how deep.
   - Hills give up stone and the common metals.
   - Mountains hold iron, silver, gold, and deeper the metals worth
     carrying home.
   - Caves are the only place crystal is found, and below nine levels down
     that means gemstones.
   - Nothing is impossible anywhere.  A hillside can hide a diamond; it is
     only unlikely.

3) Every chunk cut is a chance the face gives out.
   - Near the surface that is better than even odds.
   - The deeper you are the longer a seam lasts, and at the bottom of the
     world it is very nearly forever.

4) Metal ore goes to a crucible.  Stone and crystal wait for other hands.

See HELP MINE and HELP SMELT.
